                                       3.2 BEME Models
                                       3.2.1 Soil Phosphorus dynamics ( P )




                                                                                                                                   型
                                             We describe the dynamic process of soil P and cover the natural addition of soil P, the uptake of grass
                                       species, the natural loss of soil P, and the effects of herbicides. The change of soil P is first affected by
                                       natural recruitment, and the recruitment rate is represented by a constant λ, which represents that soil P is




                                                                                                                                 模
                                       derived from natural processes such as rock weathering and microbial decomposition. According to the
