                                       in the ecosystem and the profound effects of changing species dynamics on ecological balance. Without
                                       effective management, the removal of pesticides and herbicides can lead to negative ecological consequences,
                                       including decreased crop productivity, pest outbreaks, soil degradation, and biodiversity imbalances. These
                                       impacts highlight the importance of pesticides and herbicides in modern agricultural management and how to
                                       balance ecological conservation with agricultural production.




